## GRADING (binding, tier 2; capability decides)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the three vs main, or the counts file changed beyond its three lines or holding a conflict marker; a `simpleDb.js` hunk beyond the two sites or a site where `reject` is not inside the ROLLBACK callback, rejects with anything but the outer `err`, or lost its `return;`; the merge tree differing from the tree rule at any path but the counts file; a test added to a file other than rd973's five, an added `.skip/.only/.todo/.each`, timer or `jest.mock`; non-ASCII, a secret, a person's name or an id token in an added line; **R-INS or R-DEL green on main's `simpleDb.js`, or any of the five red at the unplanted head** (the cells do not judge the fix); **a head run of the contention loop reading 1 or more empty lists** (C4); an `afterAll` that removes a sibling it did not make, or an own `rd973-*` directory left in a seat-owned TMPDIR; the whole verify red at the head or at the landing tree per Rule S below, or a measured pair not equal to that tree's committed pair. *Major:* a plant that does not redden its predicted cell (the cell cannot fail for that fault); a builder claim your numbers contradict (the base matrix, the head matrix, the plants, 5493/326, the byte-equal blobs); **`rd913` S4 red with the empty-list symptom at the head, in the verify or in the 10 alone runs** (the ticket's done-when); a probe P1 showing a call that settles twice with different values, rejects with a value other than the original, or leaves the table not equal to the pre-state; the delivered diff beyond the commission's closed set in anything but a true comment. *Minor:* a comment sentence that is false; a test message or comment that misleads about which site a cell judges; a message sentence your transcript contradicts (Major if it hides a behaviour change); a red outside the changed files that passes alone (Rule S). *Note:* the merge subject naming the branch; the first-parent message stating the old counts pair; the DELETE-site cell proving order only; R-INS and R-DEL passing on a call that requests no ROLLBACK (R-CTL and R-ERR judge that: say which plants prove it); the contention clause NOT MET on this machine; Linux and Node 24 not run; the hosted Build and CodeQL on the PR head and on main after the merge NOT run; every `gh` read UNMEASURED; the new machine and node 26.13 against the old machine's records; the project's "never `rm` a variable path" line against the precedents (C5); a lock wait; the builder STATUS files' typos. **Rule S for a red you did not plant:** re-run it ALONE 3 times; fails alone at a branch tree at least once of 3 AND passes 3 of 3 at main's tree (`b1379-probe-base`) = Blocker; every other case is a Note with its counts (a whole-suite load timeout is a Note; the base run is the arbiter), except the S4 clause of C6. **GO** = every step measured with controls, nothing above Note; **GO WITH FINDINGS** = Minor and Note only; **NO GO** on any Blocker or Major, with class, "round 1 of 2", the fix shape in prose and that a second NO GO on this class ends it. Any required heavy job NOT RUN at the hard stop: the verdict carries `(conditional: <job> not run)`; no grade is written to fit the hour.

